212:Let $G$ be the grid graph $G=P_r\Box P_t$, with $r\geq t\geq 2$. Then $edim(G)=dim(G)=2$.
216:Since $G$ is not a path, by Remark \ref{rem-path-1}, it follows that $edim(G)\geq 2$.
264:It is already known from \cite{landmarks} that the metric dimension of grid graphs equals two. Thus, we finally get $dim(G)=edim(G)$ and the proof is completed.
