codex
A repository-level diversity check exposed one remaining design flaw before submission: the final preset’s 4×4 dimension range has only 10 torus isomorphism types, so `emit.sh` cannot produce its default 20 structurally distinct instances even though labels vary. I’m fixing the generator—not the key—by sampling many nearby cycle-size pairs while keeping their gap small, preserving G4 density and the three-label witness. Because that changes seeded instances, I will rerun all oracle arms; the existing transcripts will not be reused against changed code.
